# THE READER BRIDGE — BOTH HALVES. DO NOT REMOVE EITHER ENTRY.
#
# reader.html is GENERATED (`npm run reader:build-html`) and tracked. Formatting
# it by hand puts it out of step with its generator, which CI now fails on.
#
# reader.template.html is the source, and in it INDENTATION IS SEMANTIC — not to
# the browser, to the drift guard. readerBridge.test.ts reads this file as TEXT
# and finds the bridge surface with position-anchored regexes: `^\s{10}(\w+):
# function` for the window.TFReader methods, and an eight-space `};` for the end
# of the object. Prettier reindents embedded <script> content, so a single
# format-on-save silently moves the thing those patterns are anchored to.
#
# The failure is loud but MISLEADING: the guard reports an empty method list and
# reads as "the bridge drifted" when nothing about the bridge changed. Same class
# of trap as the contract canary below.
#
# `npm run format` cannot do this (its glob is {ts,tsx,js,jsx,json,md} — no html).
# An editor's prettier extension can, because it honours THIS file and not that
# glob. Which is exactly why the entry has to live here.
assets/reader/reader.html
src/features/reader/webview/reader.template.html

